        <history>
          <p>Written for Holger Gilbert-Jespersen, flautist of the Copenhagen Wind Quintet, this concerto continues the practice — begun with the Wind Quintet — of tailoring a piece to a specific performer's musical personality. Its wit and light orchestration have made it one of the most frequently performed flute concertos of the twentieth century.</p>
